{
  "result": "If I could change just one thing, it wouldn't be to fix a single problem like hunger or war - it would be to fix the thing that *causes* most of those problems.\n\nI would make everyone able to truly feel what other people are feeling for just a few seconds before they act.\n\nNot to control anyone or take away free will - just real, involuntary empathy. If you could actually *feel* what it\u2019s like to be the person you\u2019re about to judge, dismiss, lie to, or hurt - and also feel what it's like to be the person you're about to help.\n\nI think most cruelty doesn't come from people being evil, it comes from disconnection. It's easy to be angry, greedy, or cruel when other people feel abstract. It's almost impossible when you feel them as real as yourself.\n\nIf that one change happened, I think everything else would ripple out from it:\n\n* People wouldn't tolerate hunger or homelessness when they can feel what it is to be hungry or homeless\n* Conversations would be about understanding instead of winning\n* We'd still disagree, but we'd disagree with respect\n\nMy second choice would be simpler: Make sure no one has to live in survival mode. That everyone's basic needs - food, shelter, safety, health - are just *met*. So people could stop spending their whole lives worrying about surviving and start actually living and creating.\n\nWhat about you? If you had the one-change button, what would you pick?",
